{"author":{"id":"f21006d1826991d76b358f177209294474e8c2701fc659ff8fe8b8f40ee77f55"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774977631,"nonce":"6kv/zplSrC5QuTB/IMSFLB4fImM=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOCGKeh874NJEi","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/1142#issuecomment-4164194594"},"message":"\u003e Also it seems not to play well with Sublime Text as the text editor. It doesn't even output the \"access denied\" error message when using it. Just silently fails and shows \"Empty Title Aborting\" inside the TermUI.\n\n@rebb i believe your issue is that you have `EDITOR` set to `subl`, which is non-blocking by default (it returns immediately upon being opened). this causes the command to exit immediately, at which point the file **is** empty, because you haven't typed anything in and saved it yet.\n\n`subl` has the `--wait` (or `-w`) flag to change this behavior:\n\n```\n  -w or --wait:           Wait for the files to be closed before returning\n```\n\n`git-bug` [finds your editor][0] using the following, in order of preference (first one wins):\n\n- `GIT_EDITOR` (if set)\n- `core.editor` in your git configuration chain, if set\n- `VISUAL` (if set)\n- `EDITOR` (if set)\n- binaries in your `PATH`: `editor`, `nano`, `vim`, `vi`, `emacs`, `ed`\n\naddmitedly, we could probably support a custom variable specific to `git-bug`, but in practice, you likely want the same `subl -w` set for `GIT_EDITOR` (or `core.editor` in your git configuration).\n\n[0]: https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/blob/9b06f224354f3cf745ad6bf6620c1b04ca51077f/repository/gogit.go#L314-L354","files":null}]}